{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049970-2e-legacy-adaptation-clavicularious","id":1049970,"title":"[2e Legacy Adaptation] Clavicularious","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-16T11:55:28-08:00","id":1049970,"title":"[2e Legacy Adaptation] Clavicularious","content":"So I finally finished my 2e Clavicularious write up and I'm looking for some critique on the attainments I've written with the help of my ST and maybe some ideas for optional attainments. I left most of the history and background info the same as was printed in the 1e version, so I'll leave that out. I also ended up having to adapt a spell from the 1e book, and that is attached to this post as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Mind 2, Empathy 2, and Resolve or Composure at 3 or higher.<br /> <b>Initiation: </b>A prospective Seeker must confront his Vice demon in the astral, and resist its temptation.<br /> <b>Ruling Arcana: </b>Mind<br /> <b>Suggested Oblations: </b>The Rite of Castigation, meditation on past moments of weakness, engaging in psychological therapy (either as the therapist or as a patient). Scribing the Keys of Solomon in a durable medium.<br /> <b>Yantras: </b>Reciting the Keys of Solomon, A summoning circle, Sitting on a throne, Regalia<br /> <b>Attainment</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Insight</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Prerequisite: </b>Initiation</li> <li>After understanding his own failings, the Seeker finds himself better able to recognize the failings of others.</li> <li><b>Mechanics: </b>This attainment emulates the mind 1 spell \u201cKnow Nature\u201d with the free reach assigned to also learn the subjects Aspirations and Obsessions</li> <li><b>Optional: </b>Spirit 1, the Seeker can recognize when another\u2019s will is not their own. This optional attainment allows them to see spirits possessing others.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Urge the Demon</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Prerequisite: </b>Mind 2, Empathy 3 or Expression 3</li> <li>A Keeper-prospectus uses the knowledge gained by the previous attainment to influence another\u2019s inner demons.</li> <li><b>Mechanics: </b>This attainment emulates the mind 2 spell \u201cEmotional Urging\u201d.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Calling the Demons</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Prerequisite: </b>Mind 3, Empathy 3, Expression 2</li> <li>The Keeper preforms a great ritual, drawn from the Keys of Solomon, to call their Vice and bring it to the forefront of their mind. This allows the Solomonists to gain the benefits of indulging their Vice without actually giving in.</li> <li><b>Mechanics: </b>The mage performs a ritual emulating the spell Goetic Struggle (attached below). When presented with the opportunity to indulge his vice, the mage makes a gnosis + mind roll vs. Resolve + Composure. If the Mage wins, he regains willpower, as if he indulged his vice, without taking the action. If the Mage loses, he must indulge his vice, without regaining willpower. Reach is used to add advanced duration.</li> </ol></li> <li><b> Bind the Demons</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Prerequisite: </b>Mind 3, Spirit 4, Empathy 4, Expression 3</li> <li>The Elder-prospectus has learned the secret of Solomon. Using the Keys in a place of power in conjunction with a powerful ritual, the Elder-Prospectus binds his inner demons to fetishes to wear upon his person, removing the demon\u2019s power to influence him and gaining a measure of control over its powers.</li> <li><b>Mechanics: </b>The mage performs a ritual emulating Spirit 4\u2019s Craft Fetish, using Mind 3 conjunctive to summon a Goetia instead. The Primary factor is duration.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Suppress the Inner Demon</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Prerequisite: </b>Mind 5, Empathy 5, Expression 4</li> <li>The Elder\u2019s knowledge of Goetia and the mind allows him to completely remove the demon\u2019s influence on himself or another for 1 hour.</li> <li><b>Mechanics:</b> This emulates the Mind 5 Spell \u201cAmorality\u201d</li> </ol></li> </ol><ul><li><b>Goetic Struggle (Mind 3)</b><ul><li><b>Practice: </b>Ruling</li> <li><b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Expression, Academics, Empathy</li> </ul></li> </ul>This spell \u201csummons\u201d an inner demon into a mage\u2019s consciousness and binds it to his will. Then, whenever the mage\u2019s Vice might come into play during the spell\u2019s duration, he can mentally wrestle the demon (a contested roll between his Gnosis + Mind and his own Resolve + Composure). If he wins, he gains Willpower as if his action had reflected the Vice (even though he didn\u2019t actually act upon it). The demon is put down and banished (this spell must be cast again to gain the same effect). If the demon wins the contest, however, the mage <i>must</i> act out the Vice, and he doesn\u2019t get the Willpower for it.<ul><li><b>Optional Reach: </b><ul><li><b>+1:</b> Advanced duration</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:09:41-08:00","id":1049975,"title":"","content":"And where is Spirit Optional Attainements that let you Manifest demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:23:11-08:00","id":1050060,"title":"","content":"1st attainment takes a scene to activate as written, not sure if you knew that. Also Know Nature has to contend with Withstand so it may be ineffective on exceptional people, headsup.<br /> <br /> I don't see the point of Advanced Duration for the 3rd attainment, care to elaborate what that's for?<br /> <br /> 4th attainment requires Mind 4 for such an effect you can't create a &quot;fetish&quot; with Mind 3. Also you'd need Mind 4 just to have a 4th attainment at all.<br /> <br /> Fifth attainment as written so far takes a ritual to activate or is the Reach spent for Instant Activation? Also it can only last for 10 turns because the free Reach isn't spent on Advanced Duration. If it's supposed to be spent on Advanced Duration it will last significantly longer than an hour, one year longer in fact.<br /> <br /> Attainments seem to be a bit of a mish-mash of Mind and Spirit and should probably be better delineated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:37:12-08:00","id":1050073,"title":"","content":"Oh, also none of the attainments took into account spending Reach on Sensory Range so they must touch the target or use the attainment like an Aimed Spell in order to effect a target other than self. That includes Know Nature, Emotional Urging, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:15:49-08:00","id":1051663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049970-2e-legacy-adaptation-clavicularious?p=1049975#post1049975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where is Spirit Optional Attainements that let you Manifest demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it might be better off to get the main attainments down in stone before tackling the optionals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:25:47-08:00","id":1051671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049970-2e-legacy-adaptation-clavicularious?p=1050060#post1050060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st attainment takes a scene to activate as written, not sure if you knew that. Also Know Nature has to contend with Withstand so it may be ineffective on exceptional people, headsup.<br /> <br /> I don't see the point of Advanced Duration for the 3rd attainment, care to elaborate what that's for?<br /> <br /> 4th attainment requires Mind 4 for such an effect you can't create a &quot;fetish&quot; with Mind 3. Also you'd need Mind 4 just to have a 4th attainment at all.<br /> <br /> Fifth attainment as written so far takes a ritual to activate or is the Reach spent for Instant Activation? Also it can only last for 10 turns because the free Reach isn't spent on Advanced Duration. If it's supposed to be spent on Advanced Duration it will last significantly longer than an hour, one year longer in fact.<br /> <br /> Attainments seem to be a bit of a mish-mash of Mind and Spirit and should probably be better delineated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, so, first off, thank you so much. Second, I realized that I hadn't written in where the free reach was being spent on some of these and that was my mistake. So in order, to correct them<br /> <br /> First: free reach should be spent on instant activation, thus requiring a touch to activate.<br /> <br /> Second: free reach spent on instant activation, requiring touch.<br /> <br /> Third: the free reach was spent on advanced duration, to keep the vice bound longer, extending the effect. (This might be the mistake of a rookie player, and first time legacy designer)<br /> <br /> Fourth: You're right, it should be a mind 4 effect, emulating the Spirit 4 spell &quot;Craft Fetish&quot;, not a Spirit 4 effect using Mind 3 to work.<br /> <br /> Fifth: the free reach would be spent on instant activation and, not duration, leaving it to last 10 turns ( in my rewriting of it, I said or 1 scene, whichever is shorter).<br /> <br /> Thank you again for your help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:40:30-08:00","id":1051681,"title":"","content":"I think the third level is too much a gamble and punishes you for having high Resolve and Composure, which I find weird, making it pretty useless if you have realtively high Resistance Attributes and not very high Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:56:29-08:00","id":1051722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dman1123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049970-2e-legacy-adaptation-clavicularious?p=1051671#post1051671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so, first off, thank you so much. Second, I realized that I hadn't written in where the free reach was being spent on some of these and that was my mistake. So in order, to correct them<br /> <br /> First: free reach should be spent on instant activation, thus requiring a touch to activate.<br /> <br /> Second: free reach spent on instant activation, requiring touch.<br /> <br /> Third: the free reach was spent on advanced duration, to keep the vice bound longer, extending the effect. (This might be the mistake of a rookie player, and first time legacy designer)<br /> <br /> Fourth: You're right, it should be a mind 4 effect, emulating the Spirit 4 spell &amp;quot;Craft Fetish&amp;quot;, not a Spirit 4 effect using Mind 3 to work.<br /> <br /> Fifth: the free reach would be spent on instant activation and, not duration, leaving it to last 10 turns ( in my rewriting of it, I said or 1 scene, whichever is shorter).<br /> <br /> Thank you again for your help.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the 1st and 2nd it doesn't just have to be touch, you could also allow it to be an Aimed effect to get range which could be useful.<br /> <br /> Third attainment I think would be better with Instant Activation instead of Advanced Duration so you can just take a second to activate it whenever it might apply. Duration would last for a number of turns up to four or six turns I think.<br /> <br /> Fifth is where I'd put Advanced Duration instead of Instant Activation, and you can cancel the effect whenever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T20:18:34-08:00","id":1051827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049970-2e-legacy-adaptation-clavicularious?p=1051722#post1051722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the 1st and 2nd it doesn't just have to be touch, you could also allow it to be an Aimed effect to get range which could be useful.<br /> <br /> Third attainment I think would be better with Instant Activation instead of Advanced Duration so you can just take a second to activate it whenever it might apply. Duration would last for a number of turns up to four or six turns I think.<br /> <br /> Fifth is where I'd put Advanced Duration instead of Instant Activation, and you can cancel the effect whenever you want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, thank you again. I will update my write-up with those and will start to work on writing up some optional attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T20:21:17-08:00","id":1051830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049970-2e-legacy-adaptation-clavicularious?p=1051681#post1051681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the third level is too much a gamble and punishes you for having high Resolve and Composure, which I find weird, making it pretty useless if you have realtively high Resistance Attributes and not very high Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, did you have a suggestion for a better way to do that? My storyteller pointed out the 1e spell and I adapted it myself. For example, do you think it would be better off if I flipped it, so the Mage rolls Resolve + Composure vs. his gnosis + Mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}